1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,003
A FIFO smoke test passes, yet the design still produces a ghost output.
RTLRefine finds and replays the hidden failure before asking NVIDIA.

2
00:00:07,015 --> 00:00:16,019
This authored FIFO passes all four smoke expectations.
An independent contract finds a failure in five symbolic clock states.

3
00:00:16,083 --> 00:00:25,088
After the accepted words have left, output-valid remains asserted.
The SAT inputs reproduce this in Icarus against a separate Python queue.

4
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:56,879
A real NVIDIA Nemotron request through Nebius Token Factory.
Public source, contract and replay guide repair; final audit results stay hidden.

5
00:00:56,879 --> 00:01:08,904
Nemotron fixes occupancy when enqueue and dequeue happen together.
The exact source passes the supplied tests and final bounds 16 and 20.

6
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:36,563
Reimport and rebuild the downloaded ZIP with no new model request.
The same fixed tests, bounded properties and progress checks run again.

7
00:01:36,563 --> 00:01:44,566
The export passes again. Evidence includes source hashes and tool logs.
Progress checks exercise full, stalled, overlapping, wrapped and reset traffic.

8
00:01:44,802 --> 00:01:52,806
Change the contract: the old acceptance and checked download disappear.
A successful verdict is tied to the exact source and configuration.

9
00:01:53,181 --> 00:02:00,183
The declared eight-bit width disagrees with the four-bit DUT.
It is rejected before any paid diagnosis.

10
00:02:00,553 --> 00:02:08,556
A second authored defect passes its smoke test too.
Independent checks reproduce its premature pointer wrap in six states.

11
00:02:08,981 --> 00:02:16,984
The healthy control passes without asking the model for a repair.
These are authored integration cases, not an unseen repair-accuracy benchmark.

12
00:02:16,984 --> 00:02:23,234
Upload projects at /project; use /properties for the stated FIFO contract.
Public source and Docker test build: github.com/ehdtjq08/RTLRefine

13
00:02:23,234 --> 00:02:31,234
Patch close-up: simultaneous push and pop leave occupancy unchanged.
The exact exported file passes the fixed final bounds and progress check.

